var PLACE_INFO = {"Charminar": "Built in 1591 by Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah, the founder of Hyderabad, at the heart of the old city. Four tall minarets rise from four grand arches that face the four directions, and there is a small mosque on the upper floor. Traditionally it is linked to the end of a plague in the city. The streets around it are famous for bangles, pearls and street food.", "Golconda Fort": "Capital of the Qutb Shahi kings, built on a granite hill on the western edge of Hyderabad. The fort is known for its clever acoustics: a clap at the entrance gate can be heard at the hilltop pavilion. Golconda was also a famous diamond-trading centre. A sound-and-light show tells its story in the evening.", "Chowmahalla Palace": "The seat of the Asaf Jahi Nizams of Hyderabad, built over several decades in the 18th and 19th centuries. The name means four palaces. It has large courtyards, a long fountain pool and the Khilwat Mubarak durbar hall with its chandeliers. The palace has been restored and is open to visitors as a museum.", "Hussain Sagar": "A lake built in 1562 under Ibrahim Quli Qutb Shah, linking Hyderabad and Secunderabad. A large monolithic Buddha statue stands on an island in the middle. Tank Bund and Necklace Road run along its edge, and boat rides are popular in the evening.", "Salar Jung Museum": "One of the largest museums in India, built around the collection of Mir Yousuf Ali Khan, Salar Jung III. It holds art, sculpture, manuscripts, weapons and furniture from many countries. Visitors especially look for the Veiled Rebecca marble statue and the musical clock.", "Birla Mandir": "A temple of Lord Venkateswara built of white marble on a hill beside Hussain Sagar, completed in 1976 by the Birla Foundation. It mixes South Indian, Odisha and Rajasthani temple styles. There are no bells, and the hilltop gives wide views over the lake and the city.", "Ramappa Temple": "A Shiva temple built around 1213 CE under the Kakatiya ruler Ganapati Deva, and named after its sculptor, Ramappa. It is made of red sandstone with finely carved pillars and walls. Its UNESCO World Heritage listing came in 2021. Its tower is said to be built of very light bricks.", "Thousand Pillar Temple": "A Kakatiya temple in Hanamkonda built in 1163 CE under King Rudra Deva. It has three shrines, to Shiva, Vishnu and Surya, in a star-shaped design, with a large Nandi carved from one stone in front. Its polished, carved pillars are the highlight.", "Warangal Fort": "The fort of the Kakatiya capital. Its four stone gateways, the Kakatiya Kala Thoranam, are carved with great detail and appear in Telangana's state emblem. Ruins of the Swayambhu Shiva temple and old walls spread across the fort grounds.", "Bhadrachalam Sri Sita Ramachandra Swamy Temple": "The main Rama temple of Telangana, on the bank of the Godavari. It is linked with the devotee Bhakta Ramadasu, who built the temple in the 17th century. Sri Rama Navami is celebrated here on a grand scale, with a ceremonial wedding of Sita and Rama.", "Medak Fort": "A hill fort that began in the Kakatiya period, with strong walls and gateways. It later came under the Qutb Shahis. From the top you can see the town and the countryside around Medak.", "Medak Cathedral": "A large Gothic-style church of the Church of South India, built in the early 20th century under Rev. Charles Walker Posnett. It is known for its tall tower, big hall and stained-glass windows. It is often counted among the largest churches in Asia.", "Nagarjuna Sagar Dam": "A huge masonry dam across the Krishna river, among the largest of its kind in the world. Work started in 1955 and the dam was completed in 1967. It supports irrigation and power for both Telangana and Andhra Pradesh. The reservoir holds the island of Nagarjunakonda.", "Statue of Equality": "A 216-foot seated statue of the saint Ramanujacharya at Muchintal, unveiled in 2022. It is made of an alloy of five metals and sits on a large base with a hall of his teachings. A park around it has replicas of the 108 Divya Desam temples.", "Ramoji Film City": "A very large film studio complex near Hyderabad, recognised by Guinness as the largest in the world. Visitors can tour the film sets, gardens, shows and rides.", "Pillalamarri": "A banyan tree said to be around 700 years old near Mahabubnagar. The name means a banyan with many children, since its branches have grown into a huge shaded area. A small museum and deer park are nearby.", "Laknavaram Lake": "A Kakatiya-era lake surrounded by forested hills, with small islands and a long hanging bridge. Visitors come for boat rides and for walks on the bridge.", "Pochampally Ikat": "A weaving craft from Bhoodan Pochampally, where yarn is tie-dyed before it is woven so that bold geometric patterns appear in the cloth. It has a Geographical Indication tag, and the village was named among the world's Best Tourism Villages in 2021.", "Yadagirigutta Lakshmi Narasimha Swamy Temple": "A major hill temple of Lord Narasimha. The temple was rebuilt in dark stone and reopened in 2022 as Yadadri. Pilgrims from across Telangana come to climb the hill and worship.", "Kaleshwaram Mukteshwara Swamy Temple": "A Shiva temple known for its two lingas on a single base, one for Kaleshwara and one for Mukteshwara. It stands where the Pranahita joins the Godavari. The nearby Kaleshwaram project is a large lift irrigation scheme.", "Basar Gnana Saraswati Temple": "One of the few temples to the goddess of learning in India, on the bank of the Godavari. Parents bring young children here for the Akshara Abhyasam ceremony, which marks the start of their schooling.", "Komuravelli Mallanna Temple": "A hill temple of Lord Mallanna (Mallikarjuna Swamy) visited by large crowds from Telangana and beyond. His legends are told in the folk art of Oggu Katha. The temple is known for its annual festival with processions and folk music.", "Alampur Jogulamba Temple": "A Shakti Peetha dedicated to the goddess Jogulamba, in Alampur where the Tungabhadra meets the Krishna. It is counted among the 18 Shakti Peethas. The Navabrahma temples nearby are early Chalukya-period temples.", "Medaram Sammakka Saralamma Jatara": "A tribal festival held every two years in honour of the goddesses Sammakka and Saralamma. Lakhs of people gather in the forest at Medaram over several days. It is considered one of the largest tribal gatherings in Asia.", "Pakhal Lake": "A large lake from the 13th century, said to have been built under the Kakatiya ruler Ganapati Deva. Forest and hills surround it, and the Pakhal Wildlife Sanctuary lies around the lake.", "Kawal Tiger Reserve": "A forest reserve in the Kawal hills with teak trees, bamboo and many animals. It was notified as a tiger reserve in 2012. Visitors can go on jeep safaris.", "Kondapur Buddhist Site": "Ancient Buddhist remains from the Satavahana period, including a stupa and monastery ruins. A small museum nearby displays coins, pottery and other objects found here.", "Tirumala Sri Venkateswara Temple": "One of the most visited temples in the world, on the seven hills of Tirumala. Lord Venkateswara, also called Balaji, is worshipped here. The Tirupati laddu is a famous prasadam. The Brahmotsavam festival draws huge crowds every year.", "Kanaka Durga Temple": "A hilltop temple of the goddess Kanaka Durga on Indrakeeladri, overlooking the Krishna river in Vijayawada. The Dasara festival, when the goddess is decorated in different forms over nine days, is the biggest event of the year.", "Prakasam Barrage": "A long barrage across the Krishna river in Vijayawada, built in the 1950s and named after Andhra leader Tanguturi Prakasam. It feeds irrigation canals for the delta region and gives a fine view of the river.", "Bhavani Island": "A large island in the Krishna river near Vijayawada, reached by a short boat ride. It has gardens, a small beach and water sports, and is a popular family outing.", "Undavalli Caves": "Rock-cut caves from around the 4th to 7th century, carved out of a single hill near Vijayawada. The main cave has several storeys and a large reclining Vishnu carved from one stone.", "Amaravati Mahastupa": "A Buddhist site on the bank of the Krishna that was once one of the great stupas of India. It dates back to the Satavahana era and the Mauryan period, and its carved marble panels are now displayed in museums, including one on site.", "Nagarjunakonda": "A hill that became an island when the Nagarjuna Sagar reservoir filled. It holds Buddhist ruins of the Ikshvaku period, moved here before the flooding. A museum shows sculptures from the valley. Boats go from Vijayapuri.", "Araku Valley": "A cool hill valley in the Eastern Ghats, covered in coffee plantations and forests. Tribal communities live here, and their Dhimsa dance is a highlight. The train ride from Visakhapatnam through tunnels and hills is a favourite.", "Borra Caves": "Huge limestone caves in the Ananthagiri hills with stalactites and stalagmites in many shapes. They are lit up for visitors and are usually combined with a trip to Araku Valley.", "Lepakshi Veerabhadra Temple": "A Vijayanagara-era temple built around 1530. It is known for a large Nandi carved from a single stone, a hanging pillar that does not touch the floor, and wall paintings on the ceiling.", "Srisailam Mallikarjuna Temple": "A major temple on the Nallamala hills above the Krishna river. It is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas of Shiva and also a Shakti Peetha, where the goddess is worshipped as Bhramaramba. Pilgrims come especially for Maha Shivaratri.", "Belum Caves": "One of the longest cave systems in the Indian subcontinent, about three kilometres in all. The caves have limestone formations, passages and chambers, and traces of Buddhist and Jain monks have been found here.", "Ahobilam": "A sacred hill site in the Nallamalas with nine temples of Lord Narasimha, known as Nava Narasimha. The temples sit on the forested hills and along streams, and the pilgrimage involves some trekking.", "Kanipakam Vinayaka Temple": "A Ganesha temple beside a stream, where the idol is believed to be self-formed. Devotees come to take oaths of truth in front of the deity. Large crowds visit during Vinayaka Chaturthi.", "Srikalahasti Temple and Kalamkari": "A temple of Lord Shiva as Vayu Linga, one of the Pancha Bhoota Sthalams, with a tall gopuram. The town is also known for Kalamkari, the hand-painted textile art.", "Talakona Waterfall": "One of the tallest waterfalls in Andhra Pradesh, set in the forest of the Sri Venkateswara National Park. Visitors take a short forest walk to reach it.", "Sriharikota": "A barrier island on the coast that holds the Satish Dhawan Space Centre, ISRO's main launch site. Rocket launches are seen from a public viewing gallery on launch days.", "Arasavalli Sun Temple": "An old temple of the Sun god in Srikakulam, built in the 7th century. On two days each year the first rays of the morning sun are said to fall on the idol's feet.", "Srikurmam Temple": "A temple of Lord Vishnu in his tortoise (Kurma) form, which is rare in India. It is an old temple with inscriptions, and the main idol is shaped like a tortoise.", "Simhachalam Temple": "A hill temple near Visakhapatnam of Varaha Lakshmi Narasimha, built in the Kalinga style. The idol is covered in sandalwood paste all year and shown in its original form once a year, at Chandanotsavam.", "Kailasagiri": "A hilltop park above Visakhapatnam with sea views, a toy train and large Shiva-Parvati statues. A ropeway and roads climb the hill.", "Rushikonda Beach": "A wide golden beach near Visakhapatnam, popular for swimming and water sports such as jet-skiing and parasailing.", "RK Beach": "The main city beach of Visakhapatnam, along a long promenade. The Kursura submarine museum and the aircraft museum are close by.", "Mantralayam": "A pilgrim town on the Tungabhadra, where Sri Raghavendra Swamy took samadhi in 1671. Devotees visit his brindavan and the mutt, especially on Thursdays.", "Kondapalli Fort and Toys": "A hill fort near Vijayawada and the home of Kondapalli toys, hand-painted wooden figures made of soft wood. The toys have a Geographical Indication tag and often show village scenes.", "Etikoppaka Toys": "Wooden toys made by turning softwood on a lathe and colouring it with lacquer made from natural dyes. The craft belongs to Etikoppaka village and has a Geographical Indication tag.", "Machilipatnam Kalamkari": "A style of Kalamkari in which designs are printed with hand-carved wooden blocks and dyed with natural colours. It is practised in Machilipatnam and the nearby village of Pedana.", "Kuchipudi village": "The village in Krishna district that gave its name to Kuchipudi, the classical dance form. Its dance-drama tradition goes back many centuries, and dancers still train here.", "Gandikota": "A gorge cut by the Pennar river, often called the Grand Canyon of India. A fort, a mosque and an old temple stand on the edge of the gorge, and the views at sunrise and sunset are popular.", "Gooty Fort": "A large hill fort above the town of Gooty. Its long walls, gateways and the steep climb have made it a favourite for trekkers.", "Horsley Hills": "A cool hill station near Madanapalle, covered with eucalyptus trees and rocky viewpoints. It is a popular weekend escape from the plains.", "Madanapalle": "A town where Rabindranath Tagore stayed in 1919 and translated Jana Gana Mana into English. It is also known for its tomato market.", "Rajahmundry": "A city on the bank of the Godavari, famous for its ghats and the Godavari Arch Bridge. It is often called the cultural capital of Andhra, and is linked with the poet Nannaya.", "Dowleswaram Barrage": "A barrage across the Godavari built by Sir Arthur Cotton in the 19th century. It carries water to the Godavari delta and is credited with changing farming in the region.", "Konaseema backwaters": "A green region of canals, coconut groves and paddy fields where the Godavari meets the sea. Boat rides on the backwaters are the main attraction.", "Coringa Wildlife Sanctuary": "A mangrove forest on the Godavari delta near Kakinada. It is home to fishing cats, otters and many birds, and visitors explore it by boat.", "Annavaram Satyanarayana Temple": "A hill temple of Lord Satyanarayana on the Ratnagiri hill by the Pampa river. It is famous for its Satyanarayana Vratam, a puja that couples perform.", "Kolleru Lake": "One of the largest freshwater lakes in India, between the Godavari and Krishna deltas. Thousands of migratory birds, including pelicans, come here in winter.", "Dwaraka Tirumala": "A Venkateswara temple near Eluru, often called Chinna Tirupati. Devotees come to fulfil vows, and the temple has two idols of the deity.", "Mangalagiri": "A town with the Panakala Narasimha temple, where the deity accepts jaggery water as an offering. It is also known for Mangalagiri handloom cotton with its gold-thread borders.", "Penukonda Fort": "A hill fort that served as a capital of the Vijayanagara rulers after the fall of Hampi. It has walls, gateways, temples and a mosque.", "Puttaparthi Prasanthi Nilayam": "The ashram of Sri Sathya Sai Baba, in the village of Puttaparthi. People of many faiths visit, and the ashram is known for its free schools, hospital and water projects.", "Udayagiri Fort": "A hill fort near Nellore with ruins of old walls, temples and a mosque. It was a stronghold of Vijayanagara and later rulers, and is a trekking spot.", "Penchalakona": "A forest temple of Lord Narasimha beside a stream in the hills near Nellore. The setting is peaceful and popular with pilgrims and nature lovers.", "Bhairavakona": "Rock-cut cave temples carved into a hill in Prakasam district. They have images of Shiva and a waterfall nearby.", "Bojjannakonda and Lingalakonda": "Two Buddhist hills at Sankaram near Anakapalli, with rock-cut stupas, caves and sculptures from the early centuries CE. A short climb leads to the top.", "Salihundam": "A Buddhist monastery site on a hill beside the Vamsadhara. Stupas, monastery ruins and a museum survive from more than 2,000 years ago.", "Kalingapatnam Beach": "A quiet beach where the Vamsadhara river meets the Bay of Bengal. A lighthouse and old port ruins are nearby.", "Bavikonda and Thotlakonda": "Buddhist sites on hills near the Visakhapatnam coast. Stupas, monasteries and water tanks from about 2,000 years ago can be seen.", "Suryalanka Beach": "A long, quiet beach on the Bapatla coast, with soft sand and calm waters. It is a favourite for family trips and sunrise views.", "Mogalrajapuram Caves": "Rock-cut cave temples from around the 5th century in Vijayawada. The caves have carvings of Nataraja and other figures cut into the hill.", "Kondaveedu Fort": "A hill fort of the Reddy kings near Guntur, built in the 14th century. Its walls, gateways and old temples can be seen on a trek up the hill.", "Kotappakonda": "A hill with the Trikoteswara Swamy temple, near Narasaraopet. Its three peaks are linked to Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva. A big festival is held at Maha Shivaratri.", "Tiruchanur Padmavathi Temple": "A temple of the goddess Padmavathi, the consort of Lord Venkateswara, in Tiruchanur near Tirupati. Pilgrims are advised to visit her before going to Tirumala.", "Yaganti Uma Maheswara Temple": "A Shiva temple in a rocky setting in Nandyal district, known for its Nandi that is said to be slowly growing. Caves and a spring are nearby.", "Mahanandi": "A temple town in Nandyal district with clear spring water flowing into a pond all year. The waters are known for staying at the same level."};
(function () {
  var NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  var DEFAULTS = { tg: 'hyderabad', ap: 'visakhapatnam' };
  if (!document.getElementById('mp-style')) {
    var st = document.createElement('style');
    st.id = 'mp-style';
    st.textContent =
      '.mapgrid{grid-template-columns:1fr !important}' +
      '.mapwrap{max-width:760px;margin-inline:auto;width:100%}' +
      '.mapbox .panel{display:none}' +
      '.mp-back{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(5,8,25,.65);z-index:30;display:none}' +
      '.mp-back.on{display:block}' +
      '.mapbox .panel.mp-open{display:block;position:fixed;z-index:31;left:12px;right:12px;top:50%;' +
      'transform:translateY(-50%);max-height:84vh;overflow-y:auto;max-width:560px;margin-inline:auto;' +
      'box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.45);overscroll-behavior:contain}' +
      '.mp-x{position:sticky;top:0;float:right;z-index:3;width:40px;height:40px;margin:-6px -8px 0 8px;' +
      'border:0;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ink);color:var(--btn-fg);font:inherit;font-size:1.6rem;' +
      'line-height:1;cursor:pointer}' +
      '.mp-open .p-kicker{padding-right:44px}' +'.p-tip{margin:2px 0 0;font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}' +'.visit li{padding:0}' +'.pl{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px;width:100%;text-align:left;background:none;border:0;color:inherit;font:inherit;cursor:pointer;padding:10px 30px 10px 0;position:relative}' +'.pl::after{content:"\\203A";position:absolute;right:6px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);font-size:1.6rem;color:var(--sec)}' +'.pl:hover strong{text-decoration:underline}' +'.pd-back{font:inherit;font-weight:700;font-size:.9rem;padding:6px 12px;margin-bottom:10px;border:1.5px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);cursor:pointer}' +'.pd-text{margin-top:6px;line-height:1.6}' +'.pd-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:16px}' +'.pd-links a{text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;font-size:.92rem;padding:8px 14px;border:2px solid var(--sec-fill);color:var(--sec);border-radius:999px}';
    document.head.appendChild(st);
  }

  function el(tag, attrs, text) {
    var e = document.createElement(tag);
    if (attrs) { for (var k in attrs) { e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); } }
    if (text) { e.textContent = text; }
    return e;
  }

  function init(key) {
    var data = MAP_DATA[key];
    var host = document.getElementById('map-' + key);
    var panel = document.getElementById('info-' + key);
    var chips = document.getElementById('chips-' + key);
    if (!data || !host || !panel || !chips) { return; }

    var svg = document.createElementNS(NS, 'svg');
    svg.setAttribute('viewBox', data.viewBox);
    svg.setAttribute('role', 'group');
    svg.setAttribute('aria-label', key === 'tg' ? 'Map of Telangana districts' : 'Map of Andhra Pradesh districts');
    host.appendChild(svg);

    var paths = {};
    var buttons = {};
    var byId = {};

    data.districts.forEach(function (d) {
      byId[d.id] = d;
      var p = document.createElementNS(NS, 'path');
      p.setAttribute('d', d.d);
      p.setAttribute('class', 'dist c' + d.c);
      p.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');
      p.setAttribute('role', 'button');
      p.setAttribute('aria-label', d.name + ' district');
      var t = document.createElementNS(NS, 'title');
      t.textContent = d.name;
      p.appendChild(t);
      p.addEventListener('click', function () { select(d.id); openPop(); });
      p.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); select(d.id); openPop(); }
      });
      svg.appendChild(p);
      paths[d.id] = p;

      var b = el('button', { type: 'button', 'aria-pressed': 'false' }, d.name);
      b.addEventListener('click', function () { select(d.id); openPop(); });
      chips.appendChild(b);
      buttons[d.id] = b;
    });

    /* District name labels, placed at the centre of each district's largest piece */
    var labelGroup = document.createElementNS(NS, 'g');
    labelGroup.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
    svg.appendChild(labelGroup);

    function geom(dstr) {
      var best = null;
      dstr.split('M').forEach(function (ring) {
        var n = ring.match(/-?\d+\.?\d*/g);
        if (!n || n.length < 6) { return; }
        var pts = [];
        for (var i = 0; i + 1 < n.length; i += 2) { pts.push([+n[i], +n[i + 1]]); }
        var a = 0, cx = 0, cy = 0, x0 = 1e9, y0 = 1e9, x1 = -1e9, y1 = -1e9;
        for (var j = 0; j < pts.length; j++) {
          var p = pts[j], q = pts[(j + 1) % pts.length];
          var c = p[0] * q[1] - q[0] * p[1];
          a += c; cx += (p[0] + q[0]) * c; cy += (p[1] + q[1]) * c;
          x0 = Math.min(x0, p[0]); x1 = Math.max(x1, p[0]);
          y0 = Math.min(y0, p[1]); y1 = Math.max(y1, p[1]);
        }
        var area = Math.abs(a / 2);
        if (!best || area > best.area) {
          best = { area: area, w: x1 - x0, h: y1 - y0,
                   x: a ? cx / (3 * a) : (x0 + x1) / 2, y: a ? cy / (3 * a) : (y0 + y1) / 2 };
        }
      });
      return best;
    }

    function lines(name) {
      name = name.replace(/\s*\(.*\)/, '');
      var w = name.split(' ');
      if (w.length === 1) { return [name]; }
      if (w.length === 2) { return name.length > 11 ? w : [name]; }
      var half = Math.ceil(w.length / 2);
      return [w.slice(0, half).join(' '), w.slice(half).join(' ')];
    }

    var base = key === 'tg' ? 15 : 13;
    data.districts.forEach(function (d) {
      var g = geom(d.d);
      if (!g) { return; }
      var ls = lines(d.name);
      var longest = Math.max.apply(null, ls.map(function (l) { return l.length; }));
      var size = Math.min(base, (g.w * 0.9) / (longest * 0.56), (g.h * 0.8) / (ls.length * 1.15));
      size = Math.max(size, key === 'tg' ? 8 : 7);
      var t = document.createElementNS(NS, 'text');
      t.setAttribute('class', 'lbl');
      t.setAttribute('x', g.x.toFixed(1));
      t.setAttribute('y', (g.y - ((ls.length - 1) * size * 1.1) / 2 + size * 0.35).toFixed(1));
      t.setAttribute('font-size', size.toFixed(1));
      t.setAttribute('stroke-width', Math.max(2, size * 0.28).toFixed(1));
      ls.forEach(function (l, i) {
        var ts = document.createElementNS(NS, 'tspan');
        ts.setAttribute('x', g.x.toFixed(1));
        if (i) { ts.setAttribute('dy', (size * 1.1).toFixed(1)); }
        ts.textContent = l;
        t.appendChild(ts);
      });
      labelGroup.appendChild(t);
    });

    function slug(t) { return t.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, ''); }

    function addPhoto(folder, name, alt) {
      var fig = el('figure', { 'class': 'shot' });
      var img = el('img', { alt: alt, loading: 'lazy' });
      var exts = ['jpg', 'jpeg', 'png', 'webp'], n = 0;
      img.onerror = function () {
        if (n < exts.length) { img.src = 'images/' + folder + '/' + name + '.' + exts[n++]; }
        else { fig.remove(); }
      };
      img.onerror();
      fig.appendChild(img);
      panel.appendChild(fig);
    }

    function closeBtn() {
      var x = el('button', { type: 'button', 'class': 'mp-x', 'aria-label': 'Close' }, '×');
      x.addEventListener('click', closePop);
      panel.appendChild(x);
    }

    function renderDistrict(d) {
      panel.textContent = '';
      closeBtn();
      addPhoto('districts', d.id, d.name + ' district');
      panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-kicker' }, key === 'tg' ? 'Telangana district' : 'Andhra Pradesh district'));
      panel.appendChild(el('h3', null, d.name));
      if (d.note) { panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-note' }, d.note)); }
      panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-known' }, d.known));
      panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-head' }, 'What to visit'));
      panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-tip' }, 'Tap a place to read more.'));
      var ul = el('ul', { 'class': 'visit' });
      d.places.forEach(function (pl) {
        var li = el('li');
        var b = el('button', { type: 'button', 'class': 'pl' });
        b.appendChild(el('strong', null, pl[0]));
        b.appendChild(el('span', null, pl[1]));
        b.addEventListener('click', function () { renderPlace(d, pl); });
        li.appendChild(b);
        ul.appendChild(li);
      });
      panel.appendChild(ul);
      panel.scrollTop = 0;
    }

    function renderPlace(d, pl) {
      panel.textContent = '';
      closeBtn();
      var back = el('button', { type: 'button', 'class': 'pd-back' }, '← ' + d.name);
      back.addEventListener('click', function () { renderDistrict(d); });
      panel.appendChild(back);
      addPhoto('places', slug(pl[0]), pl[0]);
      panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-kicker' }, d.name + (key === 'tg' ? ', Telangana' : ', Andhra Pradesh')));
      panel.appendChild(el('h3', null, pl[0]));
      panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-known' }, pl[1]));
      var more = PLACE_INFO[pl[0]];
      if (more) {
        panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'p-head' }, 'About this place'));
        panel.appendChild(el('p', { 'class': 'pd-text' }, more));
      }
      var links = el('div', { 'class': 'pd-links' });
      var q = encodeURIComponent(pl[0] + ', ' + d.name + ', ' + (key === 'tg' ? 'Telangana' : 'Andhra Pradesh'));
      links.appendChild(el('a', { href: 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=' + q, target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener' }, 'Open in Maps'));
      links.appendChild(el('a', { href: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=' + encodeURIComponent(pl[0]), target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener' }, 'Read more'));
      panel.appendChild(links);
      panel.scrollTop = 0;
    }

    function select(id) {
      var d = byId[id];
      if (!d) { return; }
      Object.keys(paths).forEach(function (k) {
        var on = k === id;
        paths[k].classList.toggle('on', on);
        buttons[k].setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
      svg.insertBefore(paths[id], labelGroup);
      renderDistrict(d);
    }

    function reveal() {
      var r = panel.getBoundingClientRect();
      if (r.top < 130 || r.top > window.innerHeight - 160) {
        panel.scrollIntoView({ block: 'start' });
      }
    }
    Object.keys(paths).forEach(function (k) {
      
      
    });

    var back = el('div', { 'class': 'mp-back' });
    document.body.appendChild(back);
    var lastFocus = null;
    function openPop() {
      lastFocus = document.activeElement;
      back.classList.add('on');
      panel.classList.add('mp-open');
      panel.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
      panel.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
      panel.scrollTop = 0;
      document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
      var cb = panel.querySelector('.mp-x');
      if (cb) { cb.focus(); }
    }
    function closePop() {
      back.classList.remove('on');
      panel.classList.remove('mp-open');
      panel.removeAttribute('role');
      panel.removeAttribute('aria-modal');
      document.body.style.overflow = '';
      if (lastFocus && lastFocus.focus) { lastFocus.focus(); }
    }
    back.addEventListener('click', closePop);
    document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
      if (e.key === 'Escape' && panel.classList.contains('mp-open')) { closePop(); }
    });

    select(DEFAULTS[key]);
  }

  init('tg');
  init('ap');
})();
